<article class="env-exercise" id="02EW">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02EW">Exercise <span data-tag="02EW">111.32.5</span>.</a> Let $j : U \to X$ be an open immersion. Show that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Pullback $j^{-1} : \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (X) \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (U)$ has a left adjoint $j_{!} : \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (U) \to \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (X)$ called <em>extension by the empty set</em>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Characterize the stalks of $j_{!}({\mathcal G})$ for $\mathcal{G} \in \mathop{\mathit{Sh}}\nolimits (U)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Pullback $j^{-1} : \textit{Ab}(X) \to \textit{Ab}(U)$ has a left adjoint $j_{!} : \textit{Ab}(U) \to \textit{Ab}(X)$ called <em>extension by zero</em>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Characterize the stalks of $j_{!}({\mathcal G})$ for $\mathcal{G} \in \textit{Ab}(U)$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Observe that extension by zero differs from extension by the empty set! </p>
</article>